[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748447818","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104115#issuecomment-2748447818","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104115","id":2748447818,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j0fxK","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T15:05:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T15:05:45Z","body":"It's indeed not possible to get base scene and exposing it likely makes sense.\r\n\r\nStill, there is no proposal, so why do you need this exposed? It's not enough that something sounds useful, there needs to be a concrete use-case.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748447818/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748583220","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104115#issuecomment-2748583220","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104115","id":2748583220,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j1A00","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T15:45:27Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T15:45:27Z","body":"It is my assumption that it would be much faster to iterate through a Scene without needing to instantiate a node first. Just an assumption, though. I've had occasions where I needed to do this as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748583220/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748767008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104115#issuecomment-2748767008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104115","id":2748767008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j1tsg","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T16:43:53Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T16:44:46Z","body":"> Still, there is no proposal, so why do you need this exposed? It's not enough that something sounds useful, there needs to be a concrete use-case.\r\n\r\nRight, fair enough. I wasn't sure if it was needed for just simply binding existing methods, but I went ahead and made a proposal retroactively that hopefully explains the use-case: godotengine/godot-proposals#12061.\r\n\r\n> It is my assumption that it would be much faster to iterate through a Scene without needing to instantiate a node first. Just an assumption, though. I've had occasions where I needed to do this as well.\r\n\r\nThat's certainly another valid use-case, but that isn't the case here, as the nodes in question have already been instantiated, but as far as I can tell there is no way to get at this information even with already instantiated nodes. If scene `A` inherits from scene `B` and is then instantiated in scene `C`, there's no way to find out that the instance of `A` in `C` inherits from `B`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748767008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748991941","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104115#issuecomment-2748991941","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104115","id":2748991941,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j2knF","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T18:02:25Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T18:02:41Z","body":"> traversing the inheritance chain of said SceneState and finally emit some diagnostic based on the inheritance.\r\n\r\nThat sounds rather vague.\r\nBut still, it's something useful that can't be achieved currently, so I guess it works.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2748991941/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751805867","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104115#issuecomment-2751805867","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104115","id":2751805867,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kBTmr","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T16:15:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T16:15:16Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751805867/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753757841","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104115#issuecomment-2753757841","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104115","id":2753757841,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kIwKR","user":{"login":"ricmzn","id":6194377,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTQzNzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6194377?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn","html_url":"https://github.com/ricmzn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ricmzn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T09:37:19Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T09:38:45Z","body":"I just want to add a note that it was already possible to access the base scene before, though it was a bit implementation detail-ish.\r\n\r\nBecause inherited scenes are scenes where the root node is a scene instance, you could check what the base scene was using `state.get_node_instance(0)` (0 for the root node), which would return the PackedScene of the base scene if this scene is inherited, or null if it's not an inherited scene. \r\n\r\nI'm not opposed to this change, as I mentioned, the previous way of getting this was a bit too hidden in the API, but I'm just noting this to make sure the behavior is consistent between both methods.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753757841/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]